# Curated per-target test262 excludes for darwin/amd64, passed to run-test262
# via -x (see all_test.go). Use this file for tests that fail ONLY in the Go
# build (Go/libc numeric discrepancies) and therefore are NOT captured by the
# native C reference run in generator.go's genTargetConf. Native/upstream and
# universal excludes belong in the auto-generated test262_<os>_<arch>.conf and
# in the base test262.conf respectively.
#
# NOTE: the darwin/amd64 builder runs on the Apple-silicon (arm64) host under
# Rosetta 2 (arch -x86_64 + an amd64 Go toolchain; see cron2.sh). The libc math
# results therefore match the other amd64 targets, not darwin/arm64 -- which is
# why cosh-approx is excluded here but not in test262_exclude_darwin_arm64.

# https://gitlab.com/cznic/libquickjs/-/issues/5
# cosh-approx: last-place difference on darwin/amd64. Native C QuickJS PASSES
# this (system libm cosh); it fails only in the Go build because
# modernc.org/libc's Cosh differs from the reference constant by ~2 ULP: got
# 371.8229980468751, expected near 371.822998046875 (relative error 2).
test262/test/staging/sm/Math/cosh-approx.js

# https://gitlab.com/cznic/libquickjs/-/issues/5
# sinh-approx: the same Go/libc discrepancy already excluded on freebsd/amd64
# and darwin/arm64 (native C QuickJS PASSES; only the Go build's
# modernc.org/libc Sinh drifts a couple ULP from the reference constant): got
# 1.1667648891489082e-7, expected near 1.166764889148908e-7 (relative error 2).
test262/test/staging/sm/Math/sinh-approx.js
